# Rank 1286 / CVE-2022-44621: Apache Kylin's DiagnosisController exposes GET
# /diag/job/{jobId}/download, which hands the path-variable jobId straight to
# DiagnosisService.dumpJobDiagnosisInfo. That method builds a String[] of {
# jobId, exportPath }, joins it with spaces onto "<KYLIN_HOME>/bin/diag.sh",
# and hands the resulting string to CliCommandExecutor.execute(), which runs
# it as `bash -c <command>` (runNativeCommand). Nothing between the
# controller and the shell rejects shell metacharacters in jobId, so a jobId
# containing `; <cmd>` or a command substitution executes as the server
# (CWE-78). The fixed revision wraps the id at the controller,
# ParameterFilter.checkParameter(jobId), which strips
# `[ &`>|{}()$;\-#~!+*\\]+` before the value reaches the service.
# dumpProjectDiagnosisInfo's sibling parameter, project, passes
# through ValidateUtil.convertStringToBeAlphanumericUnderscore inside the
# service, so only the job path goes unguarded.
#
# ATTENTION. VYQL-INJ-001 (vypr.injection.Sql) fires on this file at
# both revisions, and it discriminates nothing: its finding is not the rule
# the shape actually needs. `vyql match` shows CliCommandExecutor.execute is
# labelled code.SqlExecution by binding sqlExecution96 in
# vyql/bindings/java/m420f6b67.vyql (`callee.method == "execute"`, unscoped
# by receiver type or package) -- the same method name JDBC's
# Statement/PreparedStatement use, so every "execute" call in the codebase is
# treated as a SQL sink regardless of what class defines it. There is no
# `code.CommandExecution` sink for this call at all: commandExecution125-128
# in the same file key on "exec", "ProcessBuilder", and "command", never
# "execute", so the real shell-out is invisible to VYQL-INJ-002
# (vypr.injection.Command) on both revisions. `vyql scan` on the real
# checkout confirms VYQL-INJ-001 fires at the same source (DiagnosisController
# jobId) and the same sink (DiagnosisService.java, the executor.execute(diagCmd)
# line) whether or not ParameterFilter.checkParameter runs first: its `unless
# path coveredBy core.SqlParameterization` clause asks whether the path
# excludes SQL metacharacters (quotes), and ParameterFilter's shell-oriented
# regex strips `;&|$()` but not `'` or `"`, so the clause never dominates the
# path at either revision -- a coincidentally-correct verdict (both
# revisions really are worth flagging) for the wrong reason (SQL injection,
# not command injection), that would misreport the patched revision as
# unfixed too would a complete fix leave them.
#
# No fix confined to this construct is available. A `code.CommandExecution`
# binding for CliCommandExecutor.execute, and a `core.ShellEscape` binding for
# ParameterFilter.checkParameter, would each name a class that exists only in
# Kylin's own server-base/core-common modules -- neither is a documented
# third-party API, so both fail the genericity test the same way a
# repro-shaped binding does: nobody who has not seen this CVE would write
# them from a library's documentation. Widening either binding to something
# generic (any zero-arg-named "execute" call as CommandExecution; any regex
# character-strip as ShellEscape) is a rule-wide precision change -- Java has
# no `core.ShellEscape` or `core.CommandArgumentValidation` binding at all
# today, in any file under vyql/bindings/java or vyql/bindings/packages/java
# -- and needs the OWASP command-injection corpus to judge, which is step 6's
# job, not a per-rank binding edit. No definition change attempted.
#
# verify_current_expected: attention-precision-limit, both revisions fire identically

test "rank1286: dumpJobDiagnosisInfo passes the raw path-variable jobId into the shelled-out diag command"
  lang java
  file org/apache/kylin/rest/controller/DiagnosisController.java
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.kylin.rest.controller;

  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;

  import org.springframework.stereotype.Controller;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PathVariable;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMethod;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ResponseBody;

  @Controller
  @RequestMapping(value = "/diag")
  public class DiagnosisController extends BasicController {

      private DiagnosisService dgService;

      @RequestMapping(value = "/job/{jobId}/download", method = { RequestMethod.GET })
      @ResponseBody
      public void dumpJobDiagnosisInfo(@PathVariable String jobId, final HttpServletRequest request,
              final HttpServletResponse response) {
          try (AutoDeleteDirectory diagDir = new AutoDeleteDirectory("diag_job", "")) {
              String filePath = dgService.dumpJobDiagnosisInfo(jobId, diagDir.getFile());
              setDownloadResponse(filePath, response);
          } catch (IOException e) {
              throw new InternalErrorException("Failed to dump job diagnosis info. " + e.getMessage(), e);
          }
      }
  }
  ```
  file org/apache/kylin/rest/service/DiagnosisService.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.kylin.rest.service;

  import java.io.File;
  import java.io.IOException;

  import org.apache.commons.lang.StringUtils;
  import org.apache.kylin.common.KylinConfig;
  import org.apache.kylin.common.util.CliCommandExecutor;
  import org.apache.kylin.common.util.Pair;

  public class DiagnosisService {

      public String dumpJobDiagnosisInfo(String jobId, File exportPath) throws IOException {
          String[] args = { jobId, exportPath.getAbsolutePath() };
          runDiagnosisCLI(args);
          return getDiagnosisPackageName(exportPath);
      }

      private void runDiagnosisCLI(String[] args) throws IOException {
          File script = new File(KylinConfig.getKylinHome() + File.separator + "bin", "diag.sh");
          String diagCmd = script.getAbsolutePath() + " " + StringUtils.join(args, " ");
          CliCommandExecutor executor = KylinConfig.getInstanceFromEnv().getCliCommandExecutor();
          Pair<Integer, String> cmdOutput = executor.execute(diagCmd);
      }

      private String getDiagnosisPackageName(File exportPath) {
          return exportPath.getAbsolutePath();
      }
  }
  ```

test "rank1286: the controller filters jobId for shell metacharacters, but VYQL-INJ-001 still fires on the same SQL-oriented rule"
  lang java
  file org/apache/kylin/rest/controller/DiagnosisController.java
  code
  ```
  package org.apache.kylin.rest.controller;

  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletRequest;
  import javax.servlet.http.HttpServletResponse;

  import org.apache.kylin.common.util.ParameterFilter;
  import org.springframework.stereotype.Controller;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.PathVariable;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMapping;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.RequestMethod;
  import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.ResponseBody;

  @Controller
  @RequestMapping(value = "/diag")
  public class DiagnosisController extends BasicController {

      private DiagnosisService dgService;

      @RequestMapping(value = "/job/{jobId}/download", method = { RequestMethod.GET })
      @ResponseBody
      public void dumpJobDiagnosisInfo(@PathVariable String jobId, final HttpServletRequest request,
              final HttpServletResponse response) {
          try (AutoDeleteDirectory diagDir = new AutoDeleteDirectory("diag_job", "")) {
              String filePath = dgService.dumpJobDiagnosisInfo(ParameterFilter.checkParameter(jobId), diagDir.getFile());
              setDownloadResponse(filePath, response);
          } catch (IOException e) {
              throw new InternalErrorException("Failed to dump job diagnosis info. " + e.getMessage(), e);
          }
      }
  }
  ```
  file org/apache/kylin/rest/service/DiagnosisService.java
  expect VYQL-INJ-001
  code
